me>Hargreaves</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Friedland</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Gothard</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Saxena</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Millington</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Eliahoo</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Impact on and use of health services by international migrants: questionnaire survey of inner city London A&#x00026;E attenders</article-title><source>BMC Health Serv Res</source><year>2006</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>153</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17134491</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1472-6963-6-153</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Weis</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Moonan</surname><given-names>PK</given-names></name><name><surname>Pogoda</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tuberculosis in the foreign-born population of Tarrant county, Texas by immigration status</article-title><source>Am J Respir Crit Care Med</source><year>2001</year><volume>164</volume><fpage>953</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11587977</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McCarthy</surname><given-names>OR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Asian immigrant tuberculosis &#x02013; the effect of visiting Asia</article-title><source>Br J Dis Chest</source><year>1984</year><volume>78</volume><fpage>248</fpage><lpage>53</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6743520</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McCarthy</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Interval between entry or re-entry to Britain and notification of tuberculosis among Asians in London</article-title><source>Br J Dis Chest</source><year>1984</year><volume>78</volume><fpage>248</fpage><lpage>253</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6743520</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fenton</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Chinouya</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Davidson</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Copas</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>HIV transmission risk among sub-Saharan Africans in London travelling to their countries of origin</article-title><source>Aids</source><year>2001</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>1442</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11504969</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00002030-200107270-00017</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bothamley</surname><given-names>GH</given-names></name><name><surname>Rowan</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Griffiths</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Screening for tuberculosis: the port of arrival scheme compared with screening in general practice and the homeless</article-title><source>Thorax</source><year>2002</year><volume>57</volume><fpage>45</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11809989</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/thorax.57.1.45</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>White</surname><given-names>VL</given-names></name><name><surname>Paliwalla</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Steves</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Jadhav</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Moore-Gillon</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Management of tuberculosis in a British inner-city population</article-title><source>J Public Health Med</source><year>2002</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>49</fpage><lpage>52</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11939383</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/pubmed/24.1.49</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Department of Health</collab></person-group><source>Implementing the Overseas Visitors Hospital Charging Regulations: Guidance for NHS Trust Hospitals in England</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>London: DoH</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://195.33.102.76/assetRoot/04/10/60/24/04106024.pdf"/><comment>accessed July 2005</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Department of Health</collab></person-group><source>Proposals to exclude overseas visitors from eligibility to free NHS primary medical services: a consultation</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>London: DoH</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.dh.gov.uk/en/Publicationsandstatistics/Publications/PublicationsPolicyAndGuidance/DH_4082726"/><comment>accessed August 2004</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lenz</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Bauer-Dubau</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Jelinek</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Delivery of medical care for migrants in Germany: delay of diagnosis and treatment</article-title><source>J Travel Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>133</fpage><lpage>137</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16706943</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1708-8305.2006.00030.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>HPA</collab></person-group><source>Migrant Health: Infectious diseases in non-UK born populations in England, Wales, and Northern Ireland. A baseline report &#x02013; 2006</source><year>2006</year><publisher-name>London: Health Protection Agency Centre for Infections</publisher-name></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>